      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text_908007915_copy_": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "eleni.maistrellis@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "chris.kleckner@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Sep 10 2020 13:09:36 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\"><span style=\"color: #4c7d7a;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\">Supporting pressure ulcer prevention using state-of-the-art ICU beds</span></span></span></span></span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Hospital-acquired pressure injuries (also known as pressure ulcers or bed sores) cause substantial patient harm and costs to the healthcare system. In this eGuide, discover how one hospital achieved a 91.7% decrease in hospital-acquired pressure injuries<sup>1</sup> using state-of-the-art ICU bed technology – and saved an estimated $660,000 to $5,006,100.*</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Specifically, you will also learn how:</span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Stryker’s ProCuity ZMX ICU bed and our powered Isolibrium PE support surface work together to support protocols for early mobility and pressure injury prevention.</span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">The ICU bed can become the epicenter of patient care, enhancing workflow efficiency and enabling a better experience for care teams.</span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Clinical support and data-driven partnership can help with optimizing processes and the use of ICU beds to help drive better patient outcomes.</span></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">If you’re striving to drive quality care in the ICU while navigating ongoing turnover and a less experienced staff, this eGuide is for you.</span></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Jul 16 2024 14:42:48 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0)",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
